{"ghsa_id":"GHSA-83fc-fqcc-2hmg","cve_id":"CVE-2026-23864","url":"https://api.github.com/advisories/GHSA-83fc-fqcc-2hmg","html_url":"https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-83fc-fqcc-2hmg","summary":"React Server Components have multiple Denial of Service Vulnerabilities","description":"## Impact\n\nIt was found that the fixes to address DoS in React Server Components were incomplete and we found multiple denial of service vulnerabilities still exist in React Server Components.\n\nWe recommend updating immediately.\n\nThe vulnerability exists in versions 19.0.0, 19.0.1, 19.0.2, 19.0.3, 19.1.0, 19.1.1, 19.1.2, 19.1.3, 19.1.4, 19.2.0, 19.2.1, 19.2.2, 19.2.3 of:\n\n- [react-server-dom-webpack](https://www.npmjs.com/package/react-server-dom-webpack)  \n- [react-server-dom-parcel](https://www.npmjs.com/package/react-server-dom-parcel)  \n- [react-server-dom-turbopack](https://www.npmjs.com/package/react-server-dom-turbopack?activeTab=readme)\n\nThe vulnerabilities are triggered by sending specially crafted HTTP requests to Server Function endpoints, and could lead to server crashes, out-of-memory exceptions or excessive CPU usage; depending on the vulnerable code path being exercised, the application configuration and application code.\n\n## Patches\n\nFixes were back ported to versions 19.0.4, 19.1.5, and 19.2.4.\n\nIf you are using any of the above packages please upgrade to any of the fixed versions immediately.\n\nIf your app’s React code does not use a server, your app is not affected by this vulnerability. If your app does not use a framework, bundler, or bundler plugin that supports React Server Components, your app is not affected by this vulnerability.\n\n## References\n\nSee the [blog post](https://react.dev/blog/2025/12/11/denial-of-service-and-source-code-exposure-in-react-server-components) for more information and upgrade instructions.","type":"reviewed","severity":"high","repository_advisory_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/facebook/react/security-advisories/GHSA-83fc-fqcc-2hmg","source_code_location":"https://github.com/facebook/react","identifiers":[{"value":"GHSA-83fc-fqcc-2hmg","type":"GHSA"},{"value":"CVE-2026-23864","type":"CVE"}],"references":["https://github.com/facebook/react/security/advisories/GHSA-83fc-fqcc-2hmg","https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-23864","https://react.dev/blog/2025/12/11/denial-of-service-and-source-code-exposure-in-react-server-components","https://www.facebook.com/security/advisories/cve-2026-23864","https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-83fc-fqcc-2hmg"],"published_at":"2026-01-29T15:00:30Z","updated_at":"2026-01-29T15:00:31Z","github_reviewed_at":"2026-01-29T15:00:30Z","nvd_published_at":"2026-01-26T20:16:16Z","withdrawn_at":null,"vulnerabilities":[{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"react-server-dom-parcel"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 19.0.0, < 19.0.4","first_patched_version":"19.0.4","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"react-server-dom-turbopack"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 19.1.0-canary-7130d0c6-20241212, < 19.1.5","first_patched_version":"19.1.5","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"react-server-dom-webpack"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 19.2.0-canary-63779030-20250328, < 19.2.4","first_patched_version":"19.2.4","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"react-server-dom-turbopack"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 19.0.0, < 19.0.4","first_patched_version":"19.0.4","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"react-server-dom-parcel"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 19.1.0-canary-7130d0c6-20241212, < 19.1.5","first_patched_version":"19.1.5","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"react-server-dom-parcel"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 19.2.0-canary-63779030-20250328, < 19.2.4","first_patched_version":"19.2.4","vulnerable_functions":[]},{"package":{"ecosystem":"npm","name":"react-server-dom-webpack"},"vulnerable_version_range":">= 19.1.0-canary-713